# Goal 11: Fix modf — returns 0 instead of NaN for NaN input

## Function
`modf` (double precision)

## Source Files
- C source: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/modfd.c`
- Rust source: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s5/src/mathd.rs` (fn `modfd` at line 3422)

## Problem
MISMATCH — `modf(NaN)` returns wrong value:
- C: `modf nan = nan`
- Rust: `modf nan = 0x0p+0` (returns 0.0 instead of NaN)

The NaN special case is not handled — modf should return NaN when the input is NaN.

## What Needs to Change
Add or fix the NaN check at the beginning of `modfd`. When input is NaN, both the fractional return value and the integer part (`*iptr`) should be NaN.

## Success Criteria
- `modf(NaN)` returns `NaN`
- All modf test cases match C output exactly
